      "side": 1,
      "message": "In terms of OOP design, I wish we had a `Dtc` struct that provided a Rust wrapper to the CLI tool (similar to `Command` or what\u0027s typically seen in [Rust build scripts](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/build-script-examples.html)) instead of wrapping some abstract \"DTS\" concept.\n\nA rough example of what I mean would be:\n```\nDtc::new(\"./dtc_static\")\n    .input_format(Dtc::Formats::Fs)\n    .output_format(Dtc::Formats::Dts)\n    .sorted()\n    .forced()\n    .compile(path);\n```\n\nIt would also decouple the `dtc` binary from the `rlib`, allowing the code to be re-used with other DTC builds (e.g. host?) and, as the `rlib` client would be passing the DTC path in their Rust calls, they would be less likely to \"forget\" the `data_bins` you mention in the `README`.\n\nAnyway, there\u0027s nothing prohibitively wrong with `Dts` so I won\u0027t block this CL on this comment but would appreciate it being addressed as a follow-up clean-up (feel free to create a ticket and either of us could pick it up once we get some time).",
